ty":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Sedgwick, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2d533e8d58f2bad9abad4aa09ea753e73c1301fc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2d533e8d58f2bad9abad4aa09ea753e73c1301fc.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 5 at 4:31PM MDT until September 6 at 3:00AM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northeast Colorado, including the following\ncounties, Logan County, Phillips County and Sedgwick County.\n\n* WHEN...Until 3 AM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Scattered to numerous thunderstorms are expected to repeatedly\nmove across far northeast Colorado this evening and into the\nearly morning hours. Locally, up to 3 to 5 inches of rainfall is\npossible.","ends":"2026-09-06T03:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Logan County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6974fe397cb7c06998ee1635c046b5ec68211df3.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6974fe397cb7c06998ee1635c046b5ec68211df3.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-09-05T22:44:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 052244 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 444 PM MDT Sat Sep 5 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated to scattered shower and thunderstorm activity this afternoon and again on Sunday, mainly over the mountains and our eastern plains south of Highway 50. - Better moisture moves in starting on Monday, with temperatures slowly dropping a few degrees into next","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-09-05T17:33:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 051733 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo C